  "text_pages": [
    "Housing & Life > Exchange Program | 중앙대학교 국제교류팀\nGlobal Gateway\nCAU\nExchange Program\nHOME\nExchange Program\n소개\n협정대학\nExchange Program\n파견 프로그램\nShort-Term Program\n단기 프로그램\nHousing & Life\nNotice\nOverview\nAdmission Procedures\nVisa & Immigration\nHousing & Life\nHousing & Life\n공유\nOn-Campus Housing\nOn-Campus Housing\nCampus\nSeoul\nDa Vinci\nRoom Type\nDouble Room\nQuadruple Room\nSingle Room\nDouble Room\nCost per semester\n952,000 KRW ~ 1,366,400 KRW\ndepending on the room type\n899,000 KRW ~ 1,280,000 KRW\ndepending on the room type\nThe dormitory fee may differ by semester. Meal plan is not included in the fee.\nCompliance with dormitory rules is mandatory. In the event of any violation of dormitory regulations, and if a sufficient number of negative points is accumulated, the dormitory office may require the student to vacate the dormitory.\nPlease note that the dormitory curfew is 1:00 AM.\n이전\n다음\nFacilities\nFacilities\nSeoul Campus\nDa Vinci Campus\nCafeteria\nLAN and Internet access\nComputer lab\nPhone line accessible in each room\nConvenience store and vending machines\nStudy room\nGym\nCafeteria\nLAN and Internet access\nComputer lab\nReading room\nGym\nFor more information, please refer to the dormitory website:\nSeoul campus:\nhttps://dormitory.cau.ac.kr/index.php\nDa Vinci campus:\nhttps://dorm.cau.ac.kr/index.php\nGlobal Community Center (GCC, Seoul Campus) / Global Lounge (Da Vinci Campus)\nCAU operates global lounges for international students on each campus: the Global Community Center (GCC) at the Seoul Campus and the Global Lounge at the Da Vinci Campus. International students are welcome to visit freely to meet and connect with fellow exchange students. Local CAU students also visit these spaces to interact and engage with international students.\nGlobal Ambassador (GLAM)\nCAU Global Ambassadors (GLAM) are student leaders who support CAU’s international programs, including the management of the Global Community Center (GCC), the Global Fair, and orientation programs for exchange students.\nEach exchange student is matched with a GLAM student prior to the start of the semester. GLAM students assist exchange students in settling into life in Korea and provide continuous support throughout their academic experience at CAU.\nInstagram:\n@cau_glam\nGlobal Student Internship (GSI)\nThe Global Student Internship (GSI) is an internship program that provides native speakers from around the world with opportunities to lead language lounges at the GCC, participate in global programs, and promote cross-cultural exchange. The program offers a valuable chance to connect with both local and international students while broadening your global perspectives.\nDetailed program guidelines and the application link will be shared via email at the beginning of the semester.\nMedical Assistance\nHealth Care Center is a facility dedicated to the health and well-being of students and faculty members. It provides a range of medical services, including health consultations, health education, and basic medical treatment, and is freely accessible to members of the university community.\nLocation\nSeoul: Building 310, Room B305\nDa Vinci: Building 801, Room 2108\nCAU Affiliated Hospital: 102 Heukseok-ro, Dongjak-gu, Seoul (next to the Seoul campus)\nMental Health Support and Counseling Services\nOIA supports international students experiencing psychological difficulties by identifying concerns at an early stage and providing appropriate support based on initial counseling outcomes. Through the OIA, students may be connected to a variety of extracurricular support programs or referred to professional counseling services offered by the CAU Student Counseling Center.\nThese efforts aim to promote students’ psychological well-being and help them maintain a stable and positive international student experience, including one-on-one initial counseling sessions (both online and offline), expert-led mental health support programs, and professional counseling or treatment for high-risk cases in collaboration with the Student Counseling Center.\nExchange Program\nNotice\nOverview\nAdmission Procedures\nVisa & Immigration\nHousing & Life"
